          "image",
          "Edit this picture. It is a cut-paper character on cream paper; the flat magenta areas are where his two arms (sleeves and round hands) were cut away to make a cut-out puppet. He is turned three-quarters to the viewer's left, reaching into his seed bag: his right arm was bent across his body, its sleeve down his front and its forearm and hand reaching across his chest into the mouth of the seed bag, and his left arm hung at his side beside the bag. Repaint ONLY the magenta areas, as what lies underneath his arms: on the viewer's left, his body's front outline from under the headcloth down to the robe, and across his chest the olive mantle, the walnut strap running down from his shoulder to the bag, the linen tunic, and the top of the walnut seed bag, now whole where the hand lay in its mouth; on the viewer's right, the side of his body from the armpit down to the robe, closed by the same thick dark brown-black outline as the rest of him, the olive mantle and the walnut seed bag's right edge, now whole where the hand lay beside it. Paint each in exactly the same style, colours and soft shading as his body beside the arms. Each side of his body runs straight down from the outer end of his shoulder to the outer edge of his robe below, so his body under the arms is as wide as his shoulders and his robe, and the linen tunic and olive mantle fill everything inside that line with the same soft shade and fine paper grain the sheet paints beside each arm. Keep the soft shade each arm casts on his body beside it exactly as it is, and carry that same shade on under where the arm was. Paint the linen tunic and olive mantle of his body with the same fine paper grain the sheet shows on them beside the arms: a fine, even speckle through every flat area of colour, never smooth flat colour. There are no arms now: no sleeves, no hands, nothing magenta left. Where the magenta lay outside his body, it becomes the plain cream paper. Keep every other pixel exactly as it is: the same head, headcloth and its tail, face, beard, tunic, mantle, walnut strap, belt, walnut seed bag, feet, size, position and framing.",
